(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[11 1 "// The builtins module's functions (Python/bltinmodule.c; PY5e). This file holds the functions on the"] [12 1 "// built-in types and the abstract API; the iterator types (enumerate, zip, map, filter, reversed,"] [13 1 "// callable_iterator) are builtins_iter.go's, exec/eval/compile builtins_exec.go's, __import__"] [14 1 "// import.go's. What depends on the data model's special methods of classes (format, dir's __dir__,"] [15 1 "// isinstance's __instancecheck__ ...) uses PY5c's slots and lookups when they exist."] [35 18 "// PyObject_ASCII: repr's object as it is"] [152 2 "// breakpoint (queue 304): builtin_breakpoint, sys.breakpointhook(*args, **kws)"] [164 1 "// exactArgs checks a builtin's call has n positional arguments and no keywords."] [217 2 "// builtin_print_impl's writes (queue 232): each argument's str, the separators and the end written one by one, so a"] [218 2 "// file object's write sees them as CPython's print gives them (click's tests count a stream's writes)"] [220 3 "// the standard streams encode each str with the stream's encoding and errors (queue 242: PYTHONIOENCODING, a lone"] [221 3 "// surrogate under surrogateescape), the pieces written in order into the one buffer"] [281 1 "// asciiEscape is ascii()'s escaping of a repr: every non-ASCII code point as \\x, \\u or \\U."] [323 1 "// minMax is min() and max() (min_max): the items of one iterable or of the arguments, by key, the"] [324 1 "// first extreme kept; default for an empty iterable."] [481 10 "// queue 304: PyLong_AsLongAndOverflow's overflow clamped, PyUnicode_FromOrdinal's ValueError"] [486 43 "// a lone surrogate kept (PY6c)"] [494 11 "// bytes and bytearray of one byte too (builtin_ord; PY6c)"] [508 18 "// a lone surrogate one code point (PY6c)"] [519 2 "// any int, not only a C ssize_t (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_math's msum takes bin of a 2000-bit int)"] [545 2 "// slot_nb_divmod's vectorcall_maybe: a __divmod__ or __rdivmod__ set to None is called (TypeError), queue 264"] [573 2 "// PyNumber_Power's ternary_op (PY7: the built-in did ints by int64 and an object only by its __pow__, never the"] [574 2 "// exponent's __rpow__ nor a big int)"] [628 1 "// attrName is getattr's, setattr's, hasattr's and delattr's name: a str, or a str subclass's instance as its str"] [629 1 "// value (queue 203: CPython takes any str; test_dict's test_instance_dict_getattr_str_subclass)."] [650 3 "// with a default: _PyObject_LookupAttr's lookup, a module's missing name answered without its message's work"] [651 3 "// (module_getattro's suppress: no __spec__.has_location, a Python property, called; queue 293)"] [688 3 "// a generator's StopIteration carries its return value (PY7: next() raised a bare StopIteration, the slot's"] [689 3 "// Next ending with nil)"] [708 1 "// sortObjects sorts items in place by key (nil: the items) and reverse, stably: the keys computed in"] [709 1 "// order, then PY5b's SortObjects (list.sort's)."] [762 1 "// noFrameGlobals is the globals of a call with no Python frame: the running __main__'s"] [763 1 "// (_PyEval_GetGlobalsFromRunningMain), else a new dict."] [774 1 "// frameLocals is locals() of a frame (PEP 667): a module's or class's namespace (its mapping when that is no dict;"] [775 1 "// frameNamespace), else a new dict of a function's bound fast locals, cells and free variables, then its extra locals (the proxy's"] [776 1 "// snapshot, _PyEval_GetFrameLocals: a write to it does not reach the frame)."] [779 27 "// a call with no Python frame (an interpreter's call, queue 230)"] [811 1 "// builtinDir is dir(): the scope's names, or an object's __dir__() sorted (PY5c's lookup); without a"] [812 1 "// __dir__, a module's namespace, a type's and its bases', an object's type's and its __dict__'s."] [835 3 "// the object's __dir__ (object's, type's, module's, a class's own: PY5c's), its result sorted"] [851 3 "// the scope's names: a mapping not a dict (exec's locals; queue 219) by its keys"] [856 4 "// PyMapping_Keys"] [909 2 "// the readline module imported and both streams the process's terminals (builtin_input's tty path over"] [910 2 "// PyOS_Readline, queue 289): the line by its editor, the prompt its own"] [979 1 "// roundFloat is float.__round__ (Objects/floatobject.c's double_round): to an int, ties to even, without"] [980 1 "// ndigits; else the correctly rounded value at ndigits decimal places (round-half-even on the exact decimal"] [981 1 "// value, as dtoa's mode 3), negative ndigits rounding to tens, hundreds ..."] [1003 2 "// the exact decimal value of x, rounded half-even at n places after the point"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[20 48] [26 49] [40 47] [58 46] [64 48] [74 52] [89 41] [99 48] [108 41] [121 41] [137 52] [140 32] [146 51] [186 31] [219 31] [224 39] [232 28] [236 37] [245 37] [253 43] [257 35] [262 32] [273 35] [300 46] [304 22] [314 28] [317 43] [347 34] [367 44] [422 45] [445 43] [459 43] [473 46] [490 46] [498 43] [516 45] [524 23] [538 39] [546 48] [549 49] [555 37] [584 25] [600 20] [600 28] [612 32] [639 40] [642 43] [662 37] [665 40] [678 37] [681 40] [687 34] [756 44] [767 54] [781 28] [789 37] [792 40] [798 31] [814 36] [817 39] [827 24] [836 54] [844 44] [853 25] [867 29] [882 47] [883 27] [901 38] [904 41] [911 34] [936 44] [940 33] [949 32] [1013 30]]} (go/file "builtins.go" :imports [


